11 November 2026 — Android 17 / API 37, Go QA 8087405.

Baseline 6ecb2b9: signed in through Masuk, captured a CameraX photo,
removed the test JPEG, backgrounded the app, and killed the Android process.
PID 7034 stopped. PID 7473 restored the account and opened Beranda.
The expired scan and retake controls were absent.

After the fix, repeated the same procedure. PID 10146 → 10666.
The same signed-in account saw the expired scan message. Coba lagi
opened the camera step and no photo was re-uploaded.

Repeated with the JPEG still in the cache at process death (PID 11026).
The new process (PID 11492) showed the same message, removed the stale
owner JPEG, and opened the camera step after Coba lagi. The loopback proxy
received no detection request during either process-recovery run.

